cff-version: 1.2.0
title: pulseFlesh v2.0
message: >
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Fëdor
    family-names: Zima
    email: zimanoir@gmail.com
    affiliation: Conservatorio Maderna-Lettimi Cesena Rimini
repository-code: 'https://github.com/zimanoir/pulseFlesh-v2.0'
abstract: >
  pulseFlesh v2.0 is a two-device bio-interface system developing from
  a stage-tested NIME. An independent wearable unit reads ECG and piezo
  data and is controlled by an application over Wi-Fi. A separate
  hardware sequencer, available in standalone or Eurorack format,
  receives bio-data over Wi-Fi and converts it into visualized sequences
  with physical control, wired MIDI, and CV outputs.
keywords:
  - NIME
  - DMI
  - Bio-interface
  - Wearable
  - CV Synthesis
  - Performance Art
  - Interactive Sound Design
license: MIT
